        "id": "tool:drive-the-screen",
        "listed_on": "2026-10-19T00:00:00Z",
        "label": "Operate the person's computer screen",
        "job": "Click, press, type, scroll, drag or use keys on the person's computer, finding the target by what it is called and checking afterwards what really changed",
        "description": "One call looks at the screen, finds the target, does the action, looks again and says what changed. action is one the computer keeps (tool:screen-actions lists them; new ones are added as data on the computer). Give expect, a list of { target, min?, max? } or { changed }, and verified says whether the screen shows it; without expect, verified is null and the change seen is reported. dry_run shows the steps without doing them. Press and set_value act through the accessibility tree and do not move the person's pointer; click, type and key do. A target that moved or vanished is refused, never guessed. Uses this Mac's existing Accessibility and Screen Recording permissions. The person can turn on an optional grant policy in their screen-driving settings folder; calls cannot change that policy.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "An action id from tool:screen-actions."
            },
            "target": {
              "description": "What to find on the screen: a label string, or { match: { label|role|title|description|value|identifier|text: a string or { equals | contains | starts_with | regex } }, source?: ax or ocr, nth? }. Never coordinates.",
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "object"
                }
              ]
            },
